---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = "Chengdu Travel Guide: Pandas, Spicy Food & Slow Life";
const description = "Visit Chengdu — see giant pandas, eat the world's spiciest food, and experience Sichuan's laid-back lifestyle.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">🏙️ Chengdu</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">Chengdu Travel Guide: Pandas, Spicy Food & Slow Life</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">Visit Chengdu — see giant pandas, eat the world's spiciest food, and experience Sichuan's laid-back lifestyle.</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500"><span>📅 Last updated: June 2026</span><span>⏱️ 8 min read</span></div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-50 to-red-50 border-l-4 border-orange-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-orange-900 mb-4">⚡ Quick Answer</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-orange-800 leading-relaxed">Chengdu is the <strong>land of pandas and Sichuan peppers</strong>. Watch giant pandas roll around in bamboo forests in the morning, eat food so spicy it makes your ears ring at lunch, and sip tea in a 1,000-year-old temple in the afternoon. The city is famous for its relaxed pace of life — locals say Chengdu is the "city of happiness," and you'll feel it the moment you arrive.</p>
    </div>

    <nav class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">📋 In This Guide</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        <li><a href="#why-visit" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🐼 Why Visit Chengdu?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#how-many-days" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">📅 How Many Days Do You Need?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#attractions" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🎯 Top Attractions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#getting-around" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🚇 Getting Around</a></li>
        <li><a href="#where-to-stay" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🏨 Where to Stay</a></li>
        <li><a href="#what-to-eat" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🍜 What to Eat</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="why-visit" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🐼 Why Visit Chengdu?</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-12">Chengdu is the capital of Sichuan province and the gateway to western China's natural wonders. It balances tradition and modernity effortlessly — ancient temples sit alongside trendy art districts, and the world's spiciest food is served in restaurants that have been open for generations. The pace of life is famously slow: Chengdu has more tea houses than any other city in China, and people actually use them.</p>

    <h2 id="how-many-days" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">📅 How Many Days Do You Need?</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4">
      <li><strong>3–4 days (standard):</strong> Pandas, Jinli, Wuhou Temple, and serious eating</li>
      <li><strong>5–7 days (comfortable):</strong> Add Leshan Giant Buddha (1 day) or Mount Emei (2 days)</li>
      <li><strong>7+ days (deep dive):</strong> Add Jiuzhaigou National Park (3–4 days)</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-12">If you have extra days, Sichuan province has some of the most spectacular scenery in China. The Giant Buddha at Leshan (about 1.5 hours from Chengdu) is the world's largest stone Buddha at 71 meters tall. For adventurous travelers, Jiuzhaigou's turquoise lakes and waterfalls are unforgettable but require 3–4 days minimum.</p>

    <h2 id="attractions" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🎯 Top Attractions</h2>

    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Chengdu Research Base of Giant Panda Breeding (成都大熊猫繁育研究基地)</h3><p class="text-gray-700">The best place in the world to see giant pandas up close. Go early (before 9 AM) when the pandas are most active. About 30 minutes from downtown.</p></div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Jinli Ancient Street (锦里)</h3><p class="text-gray-700">A reconstructed ancient street next to Wuhou Shrine, full of traditional architecture, snack stalls, souvenir shops, and tea houses.</p></div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Wuhou Shrine (武侯祠)</h3><p class="text-gray-700">A memorial to Zhuge Liang, the legendary strategist of the Three Kingdoms period. Visit together with Jinli in one afternoon.</p></div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Kuanzhai Alley (宽窄巷子)</h3><p class="text-gray-700">Three parallel alleyways — Wide, Narrow, and Well — restored as a pedestrian cultural district with shops, restaurants, and street performers.</p></div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">People's Park (人民公园)</h3><p class="text-gray-700">The heart of Chengdu's tea house culture. Sit at a bamboo table, order jasmine tea, and watch locals play mahjong and sing opera.</p></div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Mount Qingcheng (青城山)</h3><p class="text-gray-700">A sacred Taoist mountain about 1 hour from Chengdu. Lush bamboo forests, ancient temples, and crisp mountain air. A perfect day trip for nature lovers.</p></div>

    <h2 id="getting-around" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🚇 Getting Around</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg text-gray-700 mb-12">
      <li><strong>Subway:</strong> 6 lines covering all major attractions and the panda base. Clean, modern, and cheap. See the <a href="/en/transport/metro-bus/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Metro & Bus Guide for Major Chinese Cities</a> for general tips.</li>
      <li><strong>Didi:</strong> Very affordable — most trips across the city center are 20–40 RMB. Set it up ahead of time with <a href="/en/transport/didi/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">How to Use Didi in China as a Foreigner</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Biking:</strong> Chengdu is flat and has dedicated bike lanes. Shared bikes are everywhere.</li>
      <li><strong>High-speed rail:</strong> Chengdu East Station connects to Xi'an (3.5 hours) and Chongqing (1.5 hours). Read the <a href="/en/transport/high-speed-rail/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">How to Book and Ride China High-Speed Rail</a> for booking instructions.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="where-to-stay" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🏨 Where to Stay</h2>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Jinjiang District (锦江区) — Best for first-time visitors</h3><p class="text-gray-700">Central area around Chunxi Road and Taikoo Li. Shopping, dining, and metro connections within walking distance.</p></div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Qingyang District (青羊区) — Best for culture lovers</h3><p class="text-gray-700">Near Wuhou Shrine, Jinli, and Kuanzhai Alley. Traditional atmosphere with plenty of tea houses.</p></div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Wuhou District (武侯区) — Best for foodies</h3><p class="text-gray-700">The heart of the food scene. Walking distance to Chengdu's best restaurants and nightlife.</p></div>

    <h2 id="what-to-eat" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🍜 What to Eat</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg text-gray-700 mb-12">
      <li><strong>Mapo Tofu (麻婆豆腐)</strong> — Silky tofu in a fiery sauce of doubanjiang, chili oil, and Sichuan peppercorns.</li>
      <li><strong>Kung Pao Chicken — Gong Bao Ji Ding (宫保鸡丁)</strong> — Diced chicken with peanuts and dried chili. Sweet, sour, and spicy.</li>
      <li><strong>Dan Dan Noodles (担担面)</strong> — Noodles with minced pork, preserved vegetables, chili oil, and Sichuan pepper.</li>
      <li><strong>Hotpot — Huo Guo (火锅)</strong> — Chengdu's most social meal. A bubbling pot of spicy broth and you cook your own ingredients.</li>
      <li><strong>Twice-Cooked Pork — Hui Guo Rou (回锅肉)</strong> — Pork belly stir-fried with leeks and chili. An iconic Sichuan home dish.</li>
      <li><strong>Fuqi Feipian (夫妻肺片)</strong> — Sliced beef in chili-oil dressing with Sichuan pepper and sesame.</li>
      <li><strong>Ice Jelly — Bing Fen (冰粉)</strong> — A refreshing dessert with brown sugar syrup. The perfect palate-cooler after spicy food.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="not-prose mt-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8">📚 Related Guides</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <a href="/en/cities/city-select/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🗺️ <strong>How Many Days in China?</strong> — Plan your full itinerary</a>
        <a href="/en/cities/beijing-guide/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🏛️ <strong>Beijing Travel Guide</strong> — Compare north vs. south China</a>
        <a href="/en/payment/payment-guide/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">💳 <strong>How to Pay in China</strong> — Get your payment apps ready</a>
        <a href="/en/life/cultural-taboos/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🙏 <strong>Cultural Dos and Don'ts in China</strong> — Useful before visiting Sichuan</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>